      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T19:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should just be a Geometry and not a `const Geometry\u0026`, otherwise either the referred to object\u0027s lifetime goes away on us, or we\u0027re relying on the compiler to keep the temporary object around for us (which maybe is what happens in this case, but it doesn\u0027t seem as readable to me).\n\nFrom a performance POV, I think we\u0027ll get to the point where Device is just dealing with Geometry directly so won\u0027t have to wrap an existing Shape in a Geometry.\n\nWe could also inline this into the call to recordDraw as\n\n  recordDraw(*renderer, localToDevice, Geometry{shape}, clip, ordering, paint, stroke);\n  \nI think I prefer that way,",
