      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T19:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since Geometry is just a shape for now, this isn\u0027t critical, but SkVertices extens SkNVRefCount. Both SkNVRefCount and SkRefCount subclasses are heap-allocated objects that get passed around with the wrapping type `sk_sp\u003cFoo\u003e`, so when it\u0027s time to add SkVertices to Geometry, the union and setter/getters will be `sk_sp\u003cSkVertices\u003e`.\n\nAdditionally, for ref-counted types like this, we usually have two different getters:\n\n   SkVertices* vertices(); // or SkVertices* getVertices();\n   \nand \n\n   sk_sp\u003cSkVertices\u003e refVertices();\n   \nfor when the calling code needs to hold on to the SkVertices for longer than the Geometry object, whereas the former is used when you just need to read from the SkVertices data and can avoid the ref increment/decrement cost.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "e40be8d750fcc670fa981318b00a8ee72353f0ab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
